IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa8-helpers`

-- coa8-part15-approval.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 15, Chapter 4 (annual accounts), Approval and signing of accounts, s 414, and
-- Chapter 4A (strategic report), ss 414A and 414B (lines 5385-5417 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- The offences name "every director who" and "every person who": the directors in question are the persons the text names, not the
-- section 1121 "officer in default".

§§ `Approval and signing of accounts`

-- ---- s 414: approval and signing of accounts ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:5387 | (1) A company's annual accounts must be approved by the board of directors and signed on behalf of the board by a director of the company.
@ref s 414(1) Approval by the board and signature by a director (src:5387)
GIVEN `the accounts are approved by the board of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are signed on behalf of the board by a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 414(1) the annual accounts are approved and signed as subsection (1) requires` MEANS
    IF `the accounts are approved by the board of directors` AND `they are signed on behalf of the board by a director of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company's annual accounts must be approved by the board of directors and signed on behalf of the board by a director of the company"

-- src:5388 | (2) The signature must be on the company's balance sheet.
@ref s 414(2) The signature must be on the balance sheet (src:5388)
GIVEN `the signature is on the company's balance sheet` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 414(2) the signature is placed as subsection (2) requires` MEANS
    IF `the signature is on the company's balance sheet`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The signature must be on the company's balance sheet"

DECLARE `s 414(3) the statement the balance sheet must contain` IS ONE OF
    `s 414(3)(a) a statement that the individual accounts are prepared in accordance with the micro-entity provisions`
    `s 414(3)(b) a statement that the accounts have been prepared in accordance with the provisions applicable to companies subject to the small companies regime`

-- src:5389 | (3) If the accounts are prepared in accordance with the small companies regime, the balance sheet must contain, in a prominent position above the signature—
-- src:5390 | (a) in the case of individual accounts prepared in accordance with the micro-entity provisions, a statement to that effect, or
-- src:5391 | (b) in the case of accounts not prepared as mentioned in paragraph (a), a statement to the effect that the accounts have been prepared in accordance with the provisions applicable to companies subject to the small companies regime.
@ref s 414(3) The statement the balance sheet must contain (src:5389-5391)
GIVEN `s 381 the accounts are prepared in accordance with the small companies regime` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `they are individual accounts prepared in accordance with the micro-entity provisions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 414(3) the statement the balance sheet must contain`
`s 414(3) the statement the balance sheet must contain in a prominent position above the signature` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 381 the accounts are prepared in accordance with the small companies regime`
    WHEN JUST regime THEN
        IF regime
        THEN IF `they are individual accounts prepared in accordance with the micro-entity provisions`
             THEN JUST `s 414(3)(a) a statement that the individual accounts are prepared in accordance with the micro-entity provisions`
             ELSE JUST `s 414(3)(b) a statement that the accounts have been prepared in accordance with the provisions applicable to companies subject to the small companies regime`
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the accounts are prepared in accordance with the small companies regime"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text)

-- src:5389 | (3) If the accounts are prepared in accordance with the small companies regime, the balance sheet must contain, in a prominent position above the signature—
-- src:5390 | (a) in the case of individual accounts prepared in accordance with the micro-entity provisions, a statement to that effect, or
-- src:5391 | (b) in the case of accounts not prepared as mentioned in paragraph (a), a statement to the effect that the accounts have been prepared in accordance with the provisions applicable to companies subject to the small companies regime.
@ref s 414(3) The statement must be in a prominent position above the signature (src:5389-5391)
GIVEN `the balance sheet contains the statement the subsection requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in a prominent position above the signature` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 414(3) the balance sheet contains the statement as subsection (3) requires` MEANS
    IF `the balance sheet contains the statement the subsection requires` AND `it is in a prominent position above the signature`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the balance sheet must contain, in a prominent position above the signature"

-- src:5392 | (4) If annual accounts are approved that do not comply with the requirements of this Act ..., every director of the company who—
-- src:5393 | (a) knew that they did not comply, or was reckless as to whether they complied, and
-- src:5394 | (b) failed to take reasonable steps to secure compliance with those requirements or, as the case may be, to prevent the accounts from being approved,
-- src:5395 | commits an offence.
@ref s 414(4) Offence: approving accounts that do not comply (src:5392-5395)
GIVEN `annual accounts are approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they do not comply with the requirements of this Act` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the director knew that they did not comply, or was reckless as to whether they complied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director failed to take reasonable steps to secure compliance with those requirements or, as the case may be, to prevent the accounts from being approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 414(4) the director commits an offence` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If annual accounts are approved that do not comply with the requirements of this Act ..., every director of the company who— (a) knew that they did not comply, or was reckless as to whether they complied, and (b) failed to take reasonable steps"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where whether the accounts comply is not known and no limb decides
    `s 362 helper both answers` (JUST `annual accounts are approved`)
        (`s 362 helper both answers` `they do not comply with the requirements of this Act`
            (JUST (`the director knew that they did not comply, or was reckless as to whether they complied` AND `the director failed to take reasonable steps to secure compliance with those requirements or, as the case may be, to prevent the accounts from being approved`)))

-- src:5396 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:5397 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:5398 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 414(5) Penalties (src:5396-5398)
GIVEN conviction IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 414(5) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER conviction
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty OF conviction, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty OF conviction, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF conviction, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF conviction, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF conviction, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)

§§ `Chapter 4A: Strategic report`

-- ---- s 414B (placed before s 414A because s 414A(2) asks its answer) --------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:5415 | A company is entitled to the small companies exemption in relation to the strategic report for a financial year if—
-- src:5416 | (a) it is entitled to prepare accounts for the year in accordance with the small companies regime, or
-- src:5417 | (b) it would be so entitled but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group.
@ref s 414B Strategic report: small companies exemption (src:5415-5417)
GIVEN `s 381 the company is entitled to prepare accounts for the year in accordance with the small companies regime` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 384 the company would be so entitled but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 414B the company is entitled to the small companies exemption in relation to the strategic report` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is entitled to the small companies exemption in relation to the strategic report for a financial year if"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where a seam answer is not known and no limb decides
    `s 362 helper either answer` `s 381 the company is entitled to prepare accounts for the year in accordance with the small companies regime` `s 384 the company would be so entitled but for being or having been a member of an ineligible group`

-- ---- s 414A: duty to prepare strategic report ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:5402 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the company is entitled to the small companies exemption.
@ref s 414A(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a company entitled to the small companies exemption (src:5402)
GIVEN `s 414B the company is entitled to the small companies exemption in relation to the strategic report` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 414A(2) subsection (1) applies to the company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 414B the company is entitled to the small companies exemption in relation to the strategic report`
    WHEN JUST exempt THEN
        IF exempt
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply if the company is entitled to the small companies exemption"
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection only takes subsection (1) away from a company entitled to the exemption
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text)

-- src:5401 | (1) The directors of a company must prepare a strategic report for each financial year of the company.
@ref s 414A(1) Duty to prepare a strategic report (src:5401)
GIVEN `s 414B the company is entitled to the small companies exemption in relation to the strategic report` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 414A(1) the directors are required to prepare a strategic report for the financial year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 414B the company is entitled to the small companies exemption in relation to the strategic report`
    WHEN JUST exempt THEN
        IF exempt
        THEN `s 414A(2) subsection (1) applies to the company` (JUST TRUE) -- JUST FALSE: "Subsection (1) does not apply if the company is entitled to the small companies exemption"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is entitled to the small companies exemption (section 414B) is not known

-- src:5403 | (3) For a financial year in which—
-- src:5404 | (a) the company is a parent company, and
-- src:5405 | (b) the directors of the company prepare group accounts,
-- src:5406 | the strategic report must be a consolidated report (a “group strategic report”) relating to the undertakings included in the consolidation.
@ref s 414A(3) A group strategic report (src:5403-5406)
GIVEN `s 1173(1) in the financial year the company is a parent company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the directors of the company prepare group accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 414A(3) the strategic report must be a group strategic report relating to the undertakings included in the consolidation` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For a financial year in which— (a) the company is a parent company, and (b) the directors of the company prepare group accounts, the strategic report must be a consolidated report"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where the parent company answer is not known and no limb decides
    `s 362 helper both answers` `s 1173(1) in the financial year the company is a parent company` (JUST `the directors of the company prepare group accounts`)

-- src:5407 | (4) A group strategic report may, where appropriate, give greater emphasis to the matters that are significant to the undertakings included in the consolidation, taken as a whole.
@ref s 414A(4) A group strategic report may give greater emphasis to the significant matters (src:5407)
GIVEN `it is a group strategic report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 414A(4) the group strategic report may, where appropriate, give greater emphasis to the matters that are significant to the undertakings included in the consolidation taken as a whole` MEANS
    IF `it is a group strategic report`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A group strategic report may"

-- src:5408 | (5) In the case of failure to comply with the requirement to prepare a strategic report, an offence is committed by every person who—
-- src:5409 | (a) was a director of the company immediately before the end of the period for filing accounts and reports for the financial year in question, and
-- src:5410 | (b) failed to take all reasonable steps for securing compliance with that requirement.
@ref s 414A(5) Offence: failure to prepare a strategic report (src:5408-5410)
GIVEN `there is a failure to comply with the requirement to prepare a strategic report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was a director of the company immediately before the end of the period for filing accounts and reports for the financial year in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person failed to take all reasonable steps for securing compliance with that requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 414A(5) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `there is a failure to comply with the requirement to prepare a strategic report` AND `the person was a director of the company immediately before the end of the period for filing accounts and reports for the financial year in question` AND `the person failed to take all reasonable steps for securing compliance with that requirement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of failure to comply with the requirement to prepare a strategic report, an offence is committed by every person who— (a) was a director of the company immediately before the end of the period for filing accounts and reports for the financial year in question, and (b) failed to take all reasonable steps"

-- src:5411 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:5412 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:5413 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 414A(6) Penalties (src:5411-5413)
GIVEN conviction IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 414A(6) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    `s 414(5) the penalty on conviction` conviction
